"(PDF) Sensors in Automobiles (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/327058485_Sensors_in_Automobiles)\nciteturn282search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; \nBook PDF Available\n\n# Sensors in Automobiles\n\n  * May 2009\n\n  * Edition: 2nd\n  * Publisher: Tehran Institute of Technology Press\n  * ISBN: 978-964-354-960-2\n\nAuthors:\n\nMasoud Rezaee\n\nMasoud Rezaee\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nAmirmahyar Khorasani\n\n  * Deakin University\n\nImage\n\nDownload full-text PDFRead full-text\n\n## Abstract\n\nAlthough the desire to fly was one of the greatest aspirations of mankind, but before that, it was the move that made humans think about flying. Man has always been eager to make a device that takes him wherever he wants, and this is why the idea of starting the wheel began. Perhaps, at the time the wheel was invented, humans did not know what this invention would be, what a great transformation would be in his life. The next inventions of the wheel continued to make the car and progressed there. A device that today is one of the inseparable elements of human life. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSensors for Automotive and Aerospace Applications | Springer Nature Link (https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-981-13-3290-6)\nciteturn282search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8.0 years ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; \n\n# Sensors for Automotive and Aerospace Applications\n\n  * Book\n  * © 2019\n\n\nSensors for Automotive and Aerospace Applications\n\n## Overview\n\nEditors:\n    \n\n  * Shantanu Bhattacharya^{0},\n  * Avinash Kumar Agarwal^{1},\n  * Om Prakash^{2},\n  * …\n  * Shailendra Singh^{3}\n\n  1. Shantanu Bhattacharya\n    1. Department of Mechanical Engineering, Indian Institute of Technology Kanpur, Kanpur, India\n\nView editor publications\n\nSearch author on: PubMed   Google Scholar\n\n  2. Avinash Kumar Agarwal\n    1. Department of Mechanical